From 8969f4daa2e410a298d5c211b315157b47aeace7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 10:54:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Vulkan: reuse the graphics pipeline when none of its key's
 registers changed

FixedPipelineState::Refresh reads ~410 3D engine registers spread over the engine's state, and
GraphicsPipeline::Next then compares the whole key: ~0.5 us a draw on the PS4's Jaguar cores. The
registers Refresh reads (pipeline_key_registers.h, 412 in 103 ranges) were found by flipping every
bit of every register from random register files against fixed_pipeline_state.cpp itself, and
checked by re-randomizing all the others. Every register write (ProcessDirtyRegisters,
SinkWriteRun) now sets Maxwell3D's dirty.pipeline_key_changed when one of them takes a new value;
HLE_TransformFeedbackSetup, which writes transform_feedback_enabled directly, sets it itself.

CurrentGraphicsPipeline returns the current pipeline without refreshing the key when that flag is
clear and the engine, topology, engine state, shader hashes and squashed-blend setting are the last
lookup's, the dirty flags Refresh consumes are clear, and the last lookup found that pipeline.
Every 64th such lookup refreshes and compares instead; a difference turns the reuse off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01REmpC53sSK3VTcKMxWFSSb
